# Architecture (OpenRA2)

Read and follow `docs/architecture.md`.

## Dependency direction

`core` → `game` (World/sim) → `gfx`/`sfx` → `Game` app shell.

- `World` is deterministic simulation only.
- `Game` owns input, UI, camera, rendering, and net session glue.
- Do **not** call raylib UI/draw or play SFX from `World::applyCmd` / combat / production paths.

## God files

- Prefer putting **new** logic in `world_*.cpp` / `game_*.cpp` subsystem files.
- Do **not** add large new systems into `game.cpp` or `world.cpp`. If a change must touch them, keep it a thin call into a subsystem file.
- Keep `World::Cmd` → `applyCmd` → `update` and `checksum` semantics intact for lockstep.

## Before coding

State which layer you are changing (sim / present / app) and which file owns it per `docs/architecture.md`.
